# Byte-exactness is load-bearing in this repository.
#
# The grading fixtures under data/configs/expected/, the templates, and the
# flattened git symlinks in the capstone templates are all compared or
# interpreted as raw bytes. Git's default `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows would
# rewrite every LF as CRLF on checkout, which silently breaks all of them:
# a fixture expecting "hello\n" would arrive as "hello\r\n" and every
# comparison would fail with an identical-looking Expected/Got pair.
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion, in both directions.
* -text

# Shell tooling must stay LF so it remains executable on Unix.
*.sh text eol=lf
grade text eol=lf

# Python reverse-engineering tooling: LF keeps line numbers stable.
*.py text eol=lf
